.Sh NAME
.Nm patina-clock
.Nd the Patina desktop's clock menu
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the menu the bar's clock opens, at the bar's right end: today's date, a
month with ISO week numbers, today marked and a dot under each day with
something on, and the chosen day's events.
.Pp
The events come from the Calendar app, through
.Ql calendar --agenda ,
which reads what Calendar last synced without opening it.
A click on a day chooses it, and a double click opens Calendar at it; a
click on an event opens it in Calendar, at that day's occurrence.
The arrow keys move the chosen day, Page Up and Page Down the month, Home
goes back to today and Enter opens Calendar at the chosen day.
Escape, a click elsewhere, or the clock again closes it; running it while
one is open closes that one.
.Pp
Without Calendar it shows the month alone, and says Calendar isn't
installed.
